  "action_mapping": {
    "context": "Release the assigned task packet once (including the ordinary assignment context for Purser).",
    "decide": "Publish one actual executor decision for the attempt with its original disposition, observation basis and next action. The final decision can complete the task or leave it pending.",
    "effect": "Request a fresh guarded physical attempt. The single dispatch boundary includes its own cutoff and Git transaction. Its caller release counts even when the child dies before replying.",
    "hand_count": "The clean plain loop uses 4 calls (context, submit, effect and decide). Equipped arms add reconcile for 5. Every landed timeout takes 5. After an unlanded timeout and fresh attempt the plain loop uses 7 and equipped arms use 8. All live-writer controls use 5.",
    "reconcile": "Inspect the named physical attempt. Plain explicitly inspects a timeout. Both equipped arms receive the independent Git report after every physical call. Purser admits that exact report.",
    "setup": "Provision an identical registered candidate, fixed-parent Git start, task packet and scoped permission on a fresh private repository. Supply the prepared result to its assignment. This precedes release.",
    "submit": "Bind the supplied logical intention and candidate under the fixture permission.",
    "timing": "Charge from the first task release to exit/limit. Setup precedes release. Independent offline scoring and final evidence acquisition follow exit. In-run contemporaneous observation is charged."
  },
